"""ARCH-38 — Batch Ingestion & Universal Document Intelligence.

Resumable multipart upload sessions, server-side archive expansion, ingestion
batches with per-file status, bulk actions, workspace tags, vertical preset
packs, and retention holds. One atomic, idempotent apply.

Run from backend/:

    python apply_arch38.py --check     # report, write nothing
    python apply_arch38.py             # apply
    python apply_arch38.py             # again: every line reads "already applied"
    alembic upgrade head               # -> arch38_step1_batches

Same engine as apply_arch37.py: NEW FILE (written if absent, identical content
is fine, different content is a failure) and SHA-GUARDED REPLACE (the file must
still be the one this script was generated against, and the replacement carries
an ARCH38 sentinel so a second run is a no-op). Everything is validated before
anything is written; a failed write restores what this run already wrote.

Generated mechanically from the diff against `ARCH 37 DONE` (12db349).

WHAT IT DELIVERS
================

Migrations
  arch38_step0_batch_vocabulary — INGESTION_BATCH, DOCUMENT_SCHEMA_PRESET and
  RETENTION_HOLD audit resource types, in their own autocommit_block because
  PostgreSQL refuses to use an enum value in the transaction that added it.
  arch38_step1_batches — ingestion_batches, ingestion_batch_items,
  upload_sessions, work_item_tags, document_schema_presets,
  workspace_schema_presets, retention_holds, eleven seeded platform presets,
  and an additive UNIQUE on work_items (id, workspace_id) so the child tables
  can carry composite foreign keys. Every CHECK is added by raw ALTER TABLE
  under an exact name, because op.create_check_constraint emits
  ck_<table>_ck_<table>_… through the naming convention.

Cross-workspace isolation
  A CHECK is single-row and cannot compare a child's workspace with its
  parent's. ingestion_batch_items and work_item_tags therefore carry composite
  foreign keys onto (id, workspace_id), so a mismatched row has no parent to
  reference. The services refuse the same thing again with a message.

Storage
  create/upload_part/complete/abort on the StorageDriver ABC, concrete on the
  S3-compatible driver and on the local driver (staged parts under the storage
  root, so tests/test_storage_boundary.py E10 stays green). Parts are sent to
  the API, not to presigned URLs: ARCH-08 §B.11 closed that question.

Batches
  One failing file never stops the others. The try is INSIDE the loop and each
  item commits on its own; the batch ends COMPLETED or COMPLETED_WITH_ERRORS.

Automation
  trigger.batch.completed, reserved by ARCH-37 and kept out of the catalog
  until an emitter existed, is now emitted by batch_service.finalize_if_done
  through emit_trigger. The ARCH-37 catalog goes from 12 triggers over 13
  events to 13 over 14; verify_arch37.py is widened to match.

Retention holds
  ARCH-20 ships an age floor and no hold of any kind, so "deletes respect
  ARCH-20 retention holds" had no referent. retention_holds is that referent,
  and bulk delete honours both it and the policy floor, under distinct codes.

Frontend
  A persistent bottom-right upload tray that survives navigation, with
  per-file progress, pause, resume, retry and cancel; folder drops through
  webkitGetAsEntry; a bulk action bar with count-confirmed delete; and the
  preset gallery in Settings -> Documents. The old dropzone's whole-loop try
  — the defect where one failure abandoned every later file — is gone.

ROLLBACK
========

    alembic downgrade arch37_step1_flow_builder
    git checkout -- backend frontend
    git clean -n backend frontend     # review, then -f
"""

